ArchiveEntry "4-Machine necessity of coupling: K=0 => relative frequencies conserved, no synchronization"

/*
 * 4-machine analog of necessary_k0_3machine. With zero coupling (K=0) and zero
 * damping, each machine is fully decoupled (wi'=0), so all three relative
 * frequencies w1-w2, w2-w3, w3-w4 are individually conserved: no synchronizing
 * torque exists, the machines never pull into a common frequency. Certifies K>0
 * is necessary for synchronization. (All three relative-frequency invariants in
 * one statement.) TOPOLOGY-INDEPENDENT.
 */

ProgramVariables
  Real da; Real db; Real dc; Real dd;
  Real w1; Real w2; Real w3; Real w4;
  Real p; Real q; Real r;
End.

Problem
  w1 - w2 = p & w2 - w3 = q & w3 - w4 = r
  ->
  [{da' = w1, db' = w2, dc' = w3, dd' = w4, w1' = 0, w2' = 0, w3' = 0, w4' = 0}]
  (w1 - w2 = p & w2 - w3 = q & w3 - w4 = r)
End.

Tactic "Proof"
  implyR(1); dI(1)
End.

End.
